{
  "id": "06792_uchikesu",
  "headword": "{打|う}ち{消|け}す",
  "reading": "うちけす",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to deny, to negate",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to deny, to negate, to dismiss",
      "explanation": "To deny something that was said or claimed; to refute or contradict a statement."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to cancel out, to offset",
      "explanation": "When one thing cancels out or neutralizes the effect of another."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06792_uchikesu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{噂|うわさ}を{打|う}ち{消|け}した。",
      "english": "He denied the rumor.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06792_uchikesu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{広報|こうほう}{担当者|たんとうしゃ}は{報道|ほうどう}を{強|つよ}く{打|う}ち{消|け}した。",
      "english": "The spokesperson strongly denied the news report.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06792_uchikesu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{不安|ふあん}な{気持|きも}ちを{打|う}ち{消|け}そうとした。",
      "english": "I tried to dismiss my anxious feelings.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06792_uchikesu_ex4",
      "japanese": "{利益|りえき}が{損失|そんしつ}を{打|う}ち{消|け}した。",
      "english": "The profits offset the losses.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06792_uchikesu_ex5",
      "japanese": "{雨|あめ}の{音|おと}が{彼|かれ}の{声|こえ}を{打|う}ち{消|け}した。",
      "english": "The sound of rain drowned out his voice.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06792_uchikesu_ex6",
      "japanese": "{増収|ぞうしゅう}{分|ぶん}がコストの{増加|ぞうか}を{打|う}ち{消|け}してしまった。",
      "english": "The revenue increase was cancelled out by the rise in costs.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive).\n\nCOMPOUND VERB: Formed from {打|う}つ (to strike) + {消|け}す (to erase). The combination creates the meaning of 'striking something out' or 'erasing by striking.'\n\nGRAMMAR NOTE: In grammar, {打|う}ち{消|け}し refers to negation (e.g., {打|う}ち{消|け}しの{助動詞|じょどうし} 'negative auxiliary verb').\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{噂|うわさ}を{打|う}ち{消|け}す (deny a rumor)\n・{報道|ほうどう}を{打|う}ち{消|け}す (deny a report)\n・{疑惑|ぎわく}を{打|う}ち{消|け}す (dismiss suspicions)",
